# Cursor Editor — Rules System

## Overview

Cursor Rules are `.mdc` (Markdown Cursor) files stored in `.cursor/rules/` that provide persistent, structured guidance to the AI agent. Rules encode project standards, coding conventions, security requirements, testing patterns, and domain knowledge.

```
.cursor/rules/
├── README.mdc                    # Rules index
├── init.mdc                      # Entry point / navigation
├── context.mdc                   # Context and AI usage rules
├── architecture.mdc              # Architecture principles
├── stakeholders.mdc              # Stakeholders, goals, use cases
├── ai/
│   ├── ai-behavior.mdc           # AI behavior boundaries
│   ├── prompting-patterns.mdc    # Prompt templates
│   ├── next-actions.mdc          # Decision tree for next actions
│   ├── action-execution.mdc      # Implementation standards
│   └── project-intelligence.mdc  # Adaptive guidance system
├── compliance/
│   ├── security-rules.mdc        # Security requirements
│   └── privacy.mdc               # Privacy and data protection
├── dev/
│   ├── conventions.mdc           # Coding standards and naming
│   ├── testing-standards.mdc     # Unit, integration, E2E testing
│   ├── deployment-standards.mdc  # CI/CD, deployment procedures
│   ├── development-checklist.mdc # Development process checklist
│   ├── checklist-management.mdc  # Checklist system management
│   ├── onboarding-guide.mdc      # New team member guide
│   └── checklists/
│       ├── development-stage.mdc # Development stage checklist
│       ├── testing-stage.mdc     # Testing stage checklist
│       └── deployment-stage.mdc  # Deployment stage checklist
└── meta/
    ├── changelog.mdc             # Rule change log
    ├── index-management.mdc      # Index update rules
    └── deprecations.mdc          # Deprecated rules tracker
```

