## File Format

### Frontmatter

Every `.mdc` file requires YAML frontmatter between `---` delimiters:

```yaml
---
description: "Brief description of what this rule does (shown in rule picker)"
alwaysApply: true                    # Include in every session
globs: ["**/*.ts"]                   # File pattern for auto-attach
tags: [typescript, coding, standards] # Semantic categorization
---
```

### Frontmatter Fields

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | Yes | What the rule does; shown in rule picker |
| `alwaysApply` | boolean | No | If `true`, rule is included in every session context |
| `globs` | string[] | No | File pattern array; rule auto-attaches when matching files are referenced |
| `tags` | string[] | No | Semantic tags for categorization and retrieval |

### Body Format

After frontmatter, the file uses standard Markdown:

```markdown
# Rule Title

## Purpose
Clear explanation of what this rule does.

## Guidelines
- Specific, actionable directives
- Use clear examples
- Reference other files: @path/to/file.ts

## Examples
### Good Practice
```typescript
// ✅ Correct implementation
```
```

### Example: Complete Rule File

```markdown
---
description: "TypeScript coding standards for this project"
globs: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"]
alwaysApply: false
tags: [typescript, coding, conventions]
---

# TypeScript Coding Standards

## Error Handling

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
try {
  await fetchData();
} catch (e) {
  logger.error('Failed to fetch', { error: e });
  throw new DataFetchError('Unable to retrieve data', { cause: e });
}

// ❌ BAD
try {
  await fetchData();
} catch (e) {}
```

## Naming Conventions

- **Files**: kebab-case (e.g., `user-profile.ts`)
- **Classes**: PascalCase (e.g., `UserProfile`)
- **Functions**: camelCase (e.g., `getUserProfile`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `MAX_RETRY_COUNT`)
```

